@tradition off-the-tern
// Off the Tern (patch builder PT1, the user 2026-10-21: "the Tern brings a new junior aboard the way the player
// arrived"): on a crew rotation day (when: rotation +0) the Sunday shuttle lands its new crew at 17:40. The ramp shuts
// as the Tern comes in, Dev Raman says a word, the ramp opens and the arrivals walk down it to someone from their
// department at its foot (Zeke for Works). This brings it to the Schedule, a heads-up and Mail the evening before;
// the ramp and the walk down are section 14's rotTern (ROT_TERN). The greeter isn't counted here (section 14 plans
// them). Placeholder words by PT1 until the head writer's.
k: 454
title: Off the Tern
when: rotation +0
at: 17:35-17:55
min: 10
prio: 2
early: 5
venue: shuttle-bay
where: 5 pool @gather-shuttle-bay
hold: none
who: dept-of-honoree 40%, bunk-of-honoree 40%, everyone 5%
anim: talk
from: The Wren

== mail
- The Tern brings {names} aboard tomorrow at 17:40. Come down to the shuttle bay and say hello.

== ask
- New crew on the Tern tonight. Coming down to the bay?
- {first} lands at twenty to six. I want to be there when the ramp opens.   #warm

== here
- There's the ramp. Welcome to the Wren, {first}!   #warm
- Remember your first time down that ramp? Legs like jelly.   #funny
- Wave, everyone. Make it look like we do this every day.   #funny

== thanks
- You're in the shuttle bay to see the Tern's ramp come down for {names}. Kitbags, nervous smiles, a wave from the top.   #warm

== chatter
- New hand on the Tern today. {first}, I think.
